                <pb facs="0110" n="102" sameAs="frus:frus1941v03/pg102"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">840.48/5012: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-07-22T20:00:00+02:00">July 22, 1941—8
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received July 22—4:05 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3137. Regarding your 2703, July 21, 7 p.m., and in answer to last paragraph, I
                    made careful inquiries to make certain that studies suggested would be strictly
                    exploratory and that no position or commitments <pb facs="0111" n="103"
                        xml:id="pg103"/> would be notified without consultation with us. Also that
                    we would be kept currently informed. I very much approve the wording of the
                    reply you suggest be made to Mr. Eden and on confirmation from you will transmit
                    the same to him.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Winant</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
